// NYC taxis, rally-tracks' full bzip2 NDJSON benchmark corpus (elastic/esql-planning#1650): the complete,
// un-partitioned 165,346,692-document corpus (documents.json.bz2, 4.8GB). This migrates the disabled
// ExternalFileBzip2NdJsonCountIT#testExternalBzip2NdJsonStatsCountNycTaxisDocuments (previously
// @AwaitsFix("Very long-running test") because it has no home outside a suite explicitly designed to tolerate
// multi-hour manual runs, which this one is) -- see taxis-sample.csv-spec for the same corpus's 1,000-row
// sample, which additionally supports cross-validation and richer queries.
//
// NOT independently cross-validated: bzip2 is non-seekable (decompression must start from byte 0), and this
// object is ~10x past the ~500MB bounded-fetch allowance a DuckDB cross-check would need (plan section 6).
// The single checked-in query is a schema-agnostic COUNT(*); its expected value is the row count the
// original (disabled) internalClusterTest already documented, itself sourced from the rally-tracks NYC
// taxis track's own published corpus size, not a DuckDB/Elasticsearch run.

count_all
required_capability: dataset_in_from_command
dataset: taxis: "{{taxis}}"
FROM taxis | STATS count = COUNT(*);

count:long
165346692
;
